# E21b -- The cavern seasonal test E21 was believed to have passed. E21 reported zero out-of-season cavern arrivals and concluded the rotation holds underground — but 68 of its 70 cavern token-rows carried all four seasons, so almost nothing COULD have arrived out of season and the criterion never tested the gate. T7 then showed entry quantity gates nothing underground at all. So this runs the same question on the lever that works: five common cavern species held at frequency 1 (out of season) against the same five at 100 (in season), same fort, same window, tool disabled. Never writes a bare zero — addendum 54. A season, two replicates each.
run 20260918-153142 fort CTRL backup CTRL.preverify
DF v0.53.16 win64 STEAM DFHack 53.16-r1.1 world The Legendary Dimension site 32 tiles 29..29,20..20 seed WILDERPOP1
commits: DwarfCron ef046a3 seasonal-wildlife c8f2352 fps cap 1000

## Predictions (written before the run)
- frequency 1 is an effective out-of-season gate: near-zero arrivals of the five in the out-of-season arm and clear arrivals in the in-season arm, with total cavern life similar in both
- frequency 1 leaks: the five still arrive out of season, just less often — then a roster needs a stronger gate than 1, and the zero that would give it is unsafe
- no difference: the five arrive equally in both arms; frequency does not gate arrivals on the scale a season needs

